The reference-gain slice of the lag-by-mechanism grid: one row per institution and reporting lag at gain $0.30$, twenty seeds per cell. The reporting lag $\ell$ and the effective delay $k=\ell+1$ are shown side by side because the theory's $g^\star(k)$ refers to $k$. The full grid — ten gains × six reporting lags × six institutions, 204 cells — is in `paper/tables/main_lag_grid.csv` and in the data release, and is not reproduced here. Source: `reference_results/` (the Lead's independent reference run, cross-checked against the experiment layer in `reference_results/CROSSCHECK.md`).
 There is one reference parameterisation per institution; where the grid carries more than one gain-like parameter for an institution at the same nominal gain, only the reference one is shown here.
